.TH FATHOM_REVIEW_SIGN 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-review\-sign \- Sign an episode off, appending one entry to `.fathom/reviews/ledger.md`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom review sign\fR [\fB\-\-decision\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-identity\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIEPISODE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign an episode off, appending one entry to `.fathom/reviews/ledger.md`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-decision\fR \fI<DECISION>\fR [default: accepted]
What the decision is; `accepted` is the one that means *reviewed*
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fI<NOTE>\fR
A note, committed with the entry and folded onto one line
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Who is signing, when git config and `fathom.toml` do not say
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<AGENT>\fR
Record the act as an agent\*(Aqs verdict on someone\*(Aqs behalf, not as a human acceptance
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIEPISODE\fR>
The episode to sign off, or an unambiguous prefix of its id
